      "sourceTextSha256": "2f6920ffde2f08668080f66da73552aab26be9a6f9e41103667f0584f2a9a12b",
      "text": "Leave the hotel and head north to the Itabaca Channel, where you board a yacht for South Plaza Island. One of the smallest islands in the archipelago, South Plaza lies off the eastern tip of Santa Cruz. After an hour and a half on the water, you arrive to a red-and-green carpet of sesuvium, endemic plants scattered across the island, and the friendly barks of the resident sea lion families. The turquoise ocean contrasts with white sandy beaches and volcanic formations along the shore. It’s an easy walk past sea lions and land iguanas to the island’s highest cliff. Swallow-tailed gulls call as they swoop past, while lone male sea lions that have lost out to rivals in the competition for a harem scramble up the almost vertical rock face. Tropicbirds, blue-footed boobies and frigatebirds glide overhead. We recommend bringing binoculars for a closer look at the wildlife. From the highest point, you can look out over the ocean and watch the waves crash against the cliffs.\nContinue to Punta Carrión. Lunch is served on board. Here you can swim and snorkel alongside rays, reef sharks, Galápagos sharks and hundreds of colourful tropical fish.\nReturn to the hotel and spend the evening at your leisure.",
